4. Main Theorem — Conditional Existence of PMD

4.1 Corrected Assumptions

(A1) Spurious reliance (§3.1).

(A2′) Epistemic prior with path-measurability. There exist a non-homomorphic $\mathcal{D}_\theta$ (soft-rewrite with temperature $\beta$), a level $D_0 > 0$, and a Lipschitz constant $L_{\mathrm{TV}}$ such that for all $D \in [D_0, D_{\max}]$:

· $P_{\mathrm{sim}}(\cdot \mid do(X), \mathcal{D}_D(M))$ is $\mathcal{F}_{X_Z^\perp}$-measurable;
· the invariant mechanism $C \to Y$ is preserved;
· $\|P_{\mathrm{sim}}(\cdot \mid do(X), \mathcal{D}_{D}(M)) - P_{\mathrm{sim}}(\cdot \mid do(X), \mathcal{D}_{D'}(M))\|_{TV} \le L_{\mathrm{TV}} |D - D'|$ (Proposition 2.2).

This is a prior over which edges are spurious, tested empirically, not deduced from $M$.

(A3) Rate constraint. $|R_{PMD}| = |R_{\mathrm{retain}}| = |R_{\mathrm{abstract}}| = R$ for fixed $R$, with retention distribution-preserving.

(A4) FEC violation. $P_{\mathrm{tr}}$ violates the falsity exposure criterion.

(A5a′) Local geometry — existence. With $\epsilon(D) = \mathrm{CE}_{\mathrm{sim}}(\mathcal{D}_D(M)) - H(Y)$ continuous on $[0, D_{\max}]$ (Proposition 2.2) and $\epsilon(0) = \delta(M)$ (Corollary 3.2), there exists $D^\ast \in [D_0, D_{\max}]$ with $\epsilon(D^\ast) < \delta(M)$.

(A5b′) Local geometry — growth. There exists $D_1 \in (D^\ast, D_{\max}]$ with $\epsilon(D_1) > \delta(M)$.

(A6) Rate–transport link (§3.4).

(A7) Strict rate monotonicity. $R_c^{PMD}(D)$ is strictly decreasing on $[D_0, D_{\max}]$ (Assumption 1.16).

4.2 Corrected Definition of the Optimal Distortion Level

Definition 4.1 (Rate-constrained optimum). Define
D^\ast := \arg\min_{D \in [D_0, D_{\max}] : R_c^{PMD}(D) \le R} \epsilon(D).

This is the correction to the original Step 6: the optimal distortion must be the rate-constrained argmin, not an arbitrary $D^\ast$ satisfying $\epsilon(D^\ast) < \delta(M)$. Under (A7), the constraint is active: $R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) = R$.

4.3 Main Theorem

Theorem 4.2 (Conditional PMD existence). Under (A1), (A2′), (A3), (A4), (A5a′), (A6), (A7), there exists $D^\ast > 0$ such that
U_f(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) > \max\{U_f(M), U_f(M_{\mathrm{retain}}), U_f(A(M))\},


for every distribution-preserving $M_{\mathrm{retain}}$ and every quotient-only $A$. Hence $\mathrm{FSG}_{\mathrm{sep}}(D^\ast) > 0$ and $\mathrm{FSG}_{\mathrm{abs}}(D^\ast) > 0$.

4.4 Proof of the Main Theorem

Proof.

Step 1 (Exact memory incurs liability). By Lemma 3.1, $U_f(M) = -\delta(M)$, $\delta(M) > 0$.

Step 2 (PMD achieves invariance). By (A2′), for $D \in [D_0, D_{\max}]$, $\mathcal{D}_D(M)$ is $\mathcal{F}_{X_Z^\perp}$-measurable. By Lemma 3.4, $\mathrm{Err}_{\mathrm{spur}}(\mathcal{D}_D(M)) = 0$.

Step 3 (Total error at $D^\ast$). Define $\mathrm{Err}(\widetilde{M}) = \mathrm{CE}_{\mathrm{sim}}(\widetilde{M}) - H(Y) = -U_f(\widetilde{M})$. Under (A2′), for $D \in [D_0, D_{\max}]$, the spurious contribution vanishes, so $\mathrm{Err}(\mathcal{D}_D(M)) = \epsilon(D)$. By (A5a′), there exists $D^\ast$ satisfying Definition 4.1 with $\epsilon(D^\ast) < \delta(M)$.

Step 4 (Beats exact memory). $\mathrm{Err}(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) = \epsilon(D^\ast) < \delta(M) = \mathrm{Err}(M)$. Hence $U_f(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) > U_f(M)$ and $\mathrm{FSG}_{\mathrm{abs}}(D^\ast) > 0$.

Step 5 (Beats retention). By Lemma 3.6, $\mathrm{Err}(M_{\mathrm{retain}}) = \delta(M) > \epsilon(D^\ast) = \mathrm{Err}(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M))$. Hence $U_f(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) > U_f(M_{\mathrm{retain}})$.

Step 6 (Beats quotient-only abstraction). By Definition 4.1 and (A7), $R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) = R$ (the rate constraint is active). By Corollary 3.10,
R_c^{A}(D^\ast) \ge R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) + \Delta = R + \Delta > R.


By the definition of $R_c^A$, if $R_c^A(D^\ast) > R$, then $D^\ast$ is not achievable by class $A$ at rate $R$. Hence any $A(M)$ with $|R|(A(M)) \le R$ satisfies
\mathrm{Err}(A(M)) > \epsilon(D^\ast) = \mathrm{Err}(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)).


Therefore $U_f(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) > U_f(A(M))$.

Conclusion. Combining Steps 4–6,
U_f(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) > \max\{U_f(M), U_f(M_{\mathrm{retain}}), U_f(A(M))\},


so $\mathrm{FSG}_{\mathrm{sep}}(D^\ast) > 0$ and $\mathrm{FSG}_{\mathrm{abs}}(D^\ast) > 0$. $\square$

Remark 4.3 (Why the original Step 6 was broken). The original chain was "$R_c^A(D^\ast) \ge R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) + \Delta$ and $R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) \le R$, so $R_c^A(D^\ast) > R$." This is invalid: if $R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) = R - \Delta$, the inequality fails. The fix is Definition 4.1 (rate-constrained argmin) plus (A7) (strict monotonicity), which together force $R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) = R$.

