APPENDIX F — Full Proof of the Main Theorem

F.1 Corrected Assumptions

(A1) Spurious reliance (Section E.1).

(A2′) Epistemic prior with path-measurability. There exist non-homomorphic $\mathcal{D}_\theta$ (soft-rewrite, temperature $\beta$), a level $D_0 > 0$, and $L_{\mathrm{TV}} > 0$ such that for all $D \in [D_0, D_{\max}]$:

· $P_{\mathrm{sim}}(\cdot \mid do(X), \mathcal{D}_D(M))$ is $\mathcal{F}_{X_Z^\perp}$-measurable;
· the invariant mechanism $C \to Y$ is preserved;
· $\|P_{\mathrm{sim}}(\cdot \mid do(X), \mathcal{D}_D(M)) - P_{\mathrm{sim}}(\cdot \mid do(X), \mathcal{D}_{D'}(M))\|_{TV} \le L_{\mathrm{TV}}|D - D'|$.

(A3) Rate constraint. $|R_{PMD}| = |R_{\mathrm{retain}}| = |R_{\mathrm{abstract}}| = R$, with retention distribution-preserving.

(A4) FEC violation.

(A5a′) Existence. With $\epsilon(D) = \mathrm{CE}_{\mathrm{sim}}(\mathcal{D}_D(M)) - H(Y)$ continuous on $[0, D_{\max}]$ and $\epsilon(0) = \delta(M)$, there exists $D^\ast \in [D_0, D_{\max}]$ with $\epsilon(D^\ast) < \delta(M)$.

(A5b′) Growth. There exists $D_1 \in (D^\ast, D_{\max}]$ with $\epsilon(D_1) > \delta(M)$.

(A6) Rate–transport link (Assumption E.13).

(A7) Strict rate monotonicity. $R_c^{PMD}(D)$ strictly decreasing on $[D_0, D_{\max}]$.

F.2 Rate-Constrained Optimum

Definition F.1. Define
D^\ast := \arg\min_{D \in [D_0, D_{\max}] : R_c^{PMD}(D) \le R} \epsilon(D).

Under (A7), the constraint is active: $R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) = R$.

F.3 Main Theorem

Theorem F.2 (Conditional PMD existence). Under (A1), (A2′), (A3), (A4), (A5a′), (A6), (A7), there exists $D^\ast > 0$ such that
U_f(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) > \max\{U_f(M), U_f(M_{\mathrm{retain}}), U_f(A(M))\}


for every distribution-preserving $M_{\mathrm{retain}}$ and quotient-only $A$. Hence $\mathrm{FSG}_{\mathrm{sep}}(D^\ast) > 0$ and $\mathrm{FSG}_{\mathrm{abs}}(D^\ast) > 0$.

Proof.

Step 1. By Lemma E.1, $U_f(M) = -\delta(M)$, $\delta(M) > 0$.

Step 2. By (A2′), for $D \in [D_0, D_{\max}]$, $\mathcal{D}_D(M)$ is $\mathcal{F}_{X_Z^\perp}$-measurable. By Lemma E.5, $\mathrm{Err}_{\mathrm{spur}}(\mathcal{D}_D(M)) = 0$.

Step 3. Define $\mathrm{Err}(\widetilde{M}) = \mathrm{CE}_{\mathrm{sim}}(\widetilde{M}) - H(Y) = -U_f(\widetilde{M})$. Under (A2′), for $D \in [D_0, D_{\max}]$, $\mathrm{Err}(\mathcal{D}_D(M)) = \epsilon(D)$. By (A5a′), take $D^\ast$ as in Definition F.1 with $\epsilon(D^\ast) < \delta(M)$.

Step 4. $\mathrm{Err}(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) = \epsilon(D^\ast) < \delta(M) = \mathrm{Err}(M)$. Hence $U_f(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) > U_f(M)$ and $\mathrm{FSG}_{\mathrm{abs}}(D^\ast) > 0$.

Step 5. By Lemma E.7, $\mathrm{Err}(M_{\mathrm{retain}}) = \delta(M) > \epsilon(D^\ast) = \mathrm{Err}(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M))$. Hence $U_f(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) > U_f(M_{\mathrm{retain}})$.

Step 6. By Definition F.1 and (A7), $R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) = R$. By Corollary E.14,
R_c^A(D^\ast) \ge R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) + \Delta = R + \Delta > R.


So any $A(M)$ with $|R|(A(M)) \le R$ satisfies $\mathrm{Err}(A(M)) > \epsilon(D^\ast) = \mathrm{Err}(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M))$. Therefore $U_f(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) > U_f(A(M))$.

Conclusion. $U_f(\mathcal{D}_{D^\ast}(M)) > \max\{U_f(M), U_f(M_{\mathrm{retain}}), U_f(A(M))\}$, so $\mathrm{FSG}_{\mathrm{sep}}(D^\ast) > 0$ and $\mathrm{FSG}_{\mathrm{abs}}(D^\ast) > 0$. $\square$

Remark F.3 (Why the original Step 6 failed). The original chain "$R_c^A(D^\ast) \ge R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) + \Delta$ and $R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) \le R$, so $R_c^A(D^\ast) > R$" is invalid: if $R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) = R - \Delta$, the inequality fails. The fix is Definition F.1 (rate-constrained argmin) plus (A7), which force $R_c^{PMD}(D^\ast) = R$.

