APPENDIX H — Rate-Distortion Theory

H.1 MDL Description Length

Definition H.1. For $\widetilde{M}$ in a class $\mathcal{C}$, $|R|(\widetilde{M})$ is the minimum number of bits required to encode $\widetilde{M}$ under a fixed universal prior over $\mathcal{C}$. For episodic $M = \{e_i\}_{i=1}^n$ with $e_i \in \mathcal{E}$, and for a labeled graph $G_M = (V_M, E_M)$ with labels $\mathcal{L}$:
|R|(M) = n\ell_e, \qquad |R|(G_M) = |V_M|\log_2|V_M| + |E_M|\log_2|\mathcal{L}|.

H.2 Rate-Distortion Function

Definition H.2. For class $\mathcal{C}$ and distortion $\mathrm{Err}: \mathcal{C} \to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$,
R_c^{\mathcal{C}}(D) = \inf\{|R|(\widetilde{M}) : \widetilde{M} \in \mathcal{C}, \mathrm{Err}(\widetilde{M}) \le D, P_{\mathrm{sim}} \text{ is } \mathcal{F}_{X_Z^\perp}\text{-measurable}\}.

H.3 Properties

Proposition H.3 (Monotonicity). $R_c^{\mathcal{C}}(D)$ non-increasing in $D$.

Proof. Feasible set is nested increasing in $D$. $\square$

Proposition H.4 (Class inclusion). If $\mathcal{C}_1 \subseteq \mathcal{C}_2$, $R_c^{\mathcal{C}_1}(D) \ge R_c^{\mathcal{C}_2}(D)$.

Proof. Feasible set of $\mathcal{C}_1$ is contained in that of $\mathcal{C}_2$. $\square$

Proposition H.5 (Convexity). If $\mathcal{C}$ is closed under convex combinations and $\mathrm{Err}$ is convex, $R_c^{\mathcal{C}}(D)$ is convex in $D$ (Cover & Thomas, Ch. 10).

H.4 Rate–Transport Link (Restated)

Assumption H.6. Strictly increasing $\psi: \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0} \to \mathbb{R}_{\ge 0}$, $\psi(0) = 0$, such that if $\mathcal{C}$ forces transport cost $\ge \Delta_{\mathrm{geo}}$ on the invariant structure, then $R_c^{\mathcal{C}}(D) \ge R_c^{PMD}(D) + \psi(\Delta_{\mathrm{geo}})$ for $D \ge D_0$.

Remark H.7 (Falsifiability). If one exhibits a quotient-only $A$ achieving the same rate-distortion profile as PMD despite $\Delta_{\mathrm{geo}} > 0$, H.6 is refuted.

